From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] ship the bundled llhttp licence in the wheel

setup.py compiles llhttp/src/{api,http,llhttp}.c straight into
geventhttpclient._parser, so every wheel redistributes llhttp (MIT,
Copyright Fedor Indutny) in binary form. The MIT licence requires that
notice to travel with the binary, but only the project's own root
LICENSE-MIT is picked up by the default license-files globs, so
llhttp/LICENSE-MIT never reaches dist-info/licenses/.

Declaring license-files explicitly ships both. PEP 639 preserves each
entry's path relative to the project root, so llhttp's copy lands at
dist-info/licenses/llhttp/LICENSE-MIT next to the project's own.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; no fork of geventhttpclient/geventhttpclient to push from]
---
 pyproject.toml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ description = "HTTP client library for gevent"
 readme = "README.md"
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
 license = "MIT"
+license-files = ["LICENSE-MIT", "llhttp/LICENSE-MIT"]
 keywords = ["http", "gevent", "client"]
 authors = [{name = "Antonin Amand", email = "antonin.amand@gmail.com"}]
 classifiers = [
